# Backend Rules

- Follow the existing Node.js and Express architecture.
- Inspect existing routes, controllers, services, and middleware first.
- Keep business logic in the appropriate service layer.
- Validate incoming request data.
- Enforce authentication and authorization server-side.
- Verify resource ownership for user and provider operations.
- Keep external API credentials on the server.
- Handle AI provider errors, timeouts, and unavailable services.
- Provide a deterministic mock AI adapter for demo mode when needed.
- Do not return sensitive information in API responses.
- Use consistent error handling.
- Do not introduce another backend framework.
- Do not claim an integration is live when it is mocked.
